From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shu Zhao <shuzhao.cs@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 11:48:09 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(session): flatten text-only content-part lists like
 SGLang

Agent harnesses such as ProRL's OpenHands fork send message content in
the OpenAI list form ([{"type": "text", "text": ...}]). SGLang renders a
text-only list as the space-joined string, but the TITO templates read
string content only: Qwen3's template concatenates a system message's
content as a string, so a list there fails the render (a TypeError, so
every OpenHands turn got a 500), and other list content renders as ''.
The session also matches stored history against string content.

flatten_text_part_messages flattens text-only part lists to that string;
any other content passes through. resolve_request_args_by_config applies
it to the forwarded body with the other server rules, and both session
versions apply it to the messages they match history against and render
input_ids from.

The client-reply half of the former session-client-view patch (no
logprobs / meta_info unless asked) is upstream since #3877 and #3716.
